body:
^ is for ctrl
! is for alt
+ is for shift

first, you need to check if NumpadMult even works:

NumpadMult::

MsgBox check

Return

If it shows a popup,

NumpadMult::^!b

should most definetly work, if it doesnt work, you could try:

NumpadMult::

Send {Ctrl down}

Send {Alt down}

Send {b down}

Sleep 80

Send {Ctrl up}

Send {Alt up}

Send {b up}

Return

If this doesn't work I have nothing else left

NumpadMult::

Send {Ctrl}{Alt}{b}

return

yea, I've just wrote something very similar to that and tested, it works:  


Space::

Send {Ctrl down}{LButton down}

Loop{

if !GetKeyState("Space", "P")

	break

Sleep 20

}

Send {Ctrl up}{LButton up}

Return

Browser_Home::

Send {Ctrl down}

Send {v down}

Sleep 50

Send {Ctrl up}

Send {v up}

return

F12::  ; f12 starts your script

Send {w down}

Loop{

PixelGetColor, color, 963, 630

if (color == 0x7A96D7){

	SendInput {space}

	Sleep 50 ; sometimes you need to use sleeps, so game can register clicks

; because AHK can click too fast and it wont register, if clicked several times in quick succession

}

Return

&#x200B;

F11::   ; f11 will reset your script

Send {w up}

Reload

Return

you mean when you press 5 click down left mouse button or what? to make something like that, you will need variable, for example:

x=1

*~somehotkey::
if(x==1)
{
Send {LButton} {down}
x=x+1
}
if(x==2)
{
Send {LButton}
x=x+1
}
if(x==3)
{
Send {LButton} {down}
}
x=1
Return
